{"step_index":222,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-30T06:15:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-30T11:45:59+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-30T11:45:59+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/brain/b1401ff7-7a8f-4c14-be76-c6f41632d249/student_survival_app_showcase.md`\nTotal Lines: 110\nTotal Bytes: 5758\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🎓 Student Survival App 🧑‍🎓🔥\n2: > **Tagline:** *“Survive college. One deadline at a time. 😂”*  \n3: > **Subtitle:** *“Because college is already hard enough 😭”*  \n4: > **Status:** Fully Functional & Ready to Run\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 🖼️ Application Visual Identity\n9: \n10: The uploaded **“Life of a Student”** hand-drawn notebook illustration is the core aesthetic foundation of the entire app: [life-of-a-student.jpg](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/student-survival-app/assets/life-of-a-student.jpg)\n11: \n12: ### Dual Implementation:\n13: 1. **App Icon & Logo Crop**:\n14:    - Styled as a rounded-square badge with subtle gradient glow and shadow.\n15:    - Featured on the **Animated Loading Splash Screen**, the **Glassmorphism Login Card**, the **Top Sticky Navigation Header**, and the **Student Profile**.\n16: 2. **Full-Screen Fixed Background**:\n17:    - Styled with `background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-attachment: fixed;`.\n18:    - Covered with a dark translucent glassmorphic overlay (`backdrop-filter: blur(16px)`), ensuring all text, badges, and progress bars maintain AAA contrast while keeping the spiral notebook, pencils, ruler, crushed student, and teacher recognizable in the background.\n19:    - On mobile screens, smartly anchored so the notebook title and key illustration remain in focus.\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## 🏗️ System Architecture & Workflow\n24: \n25: ```mermaid\n26: flowchart TD\n27:     A[\"🚀 App Launch (index.html)\"] --> B[\"⏳ Animated Splash (2.5s)\"]\n28:     B -->|Check localStorage Session| C{\"User Remembered?\"}\n29:     C -->|No| D[\"🔐 Glassmorphic Login / Guest Mode\"]\n30:     C -->|Yes| E[\"🏠 Home Survival Dashboard\"]\n31:     D -->|Submit / Guest Click| E\n32:     \n33:     E --> F[\"📊 Attendance Engine (75% Math)\"]\n34:     E --> G[\"📝 Assignment Countdown (Sorted Deadlines)\"]\n35:     E --> H[\"🍔 Campus Canteen (Status & Price Calculator)\"]\n36:     E --> I[\"📅 Weekly Timetable (Auto Current Day)\"]\n37:     E --> J[\"⏳ Exam Countdown (Live Seconds Ticker)\"]\n38:     E --> K[\"😂 Should I Sleep or Study? (Survival AI)\"]\n39: \n40:     F --> L[\"💾 Browser localStorage (Persistent State)\"]\n41:     G --> L\n42:     H --> L\n43:     I --> L\n44:     J --> L\n45:     K --> M[\"⏱️ 20-Minute Power Nap Timer & Alarm\"]\n46: ```\n47: \n48: ---\n49: \n50: ## ⚡ Quick Launch Guide\n51: \n52: > [!TIP]\n53: > The app is 100% client-side with zero build steps or external package dependencies required.\n54: \n55: You can launch and test the app from either location:\n56: \n57: | Location | Path | Usage |\n58: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n59: | **Workspace (Recommended)** | [`student-survival-app/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/DELL/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/student-survival-app/index.html) | Main working directory |\n60: | **Desktop Shortcut** | [`student-survival-app/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/DELL/OneDrive/Desktop/student%20survival/student-survival-app/index.html) | Direct desktop launcher |\n61: \n62: ### To Run:\n63: - Double-click **`index.html`** to open in **Google Chrome**, **Microsoft Edge**, **Brave**, **Firefox**, or **Safari**.\n64: - Use the **Skip to App** button on the splash screen or wait ~2.5 seconds to experience the animated collegiate quotes.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 🧮 Core Engines & Mathematical Formulas\n69: \n70: ### 1. Attendance Bunk & Shortage Engine\n71: - **Attendance Percentage**:\n72:   $$\\text{Attendance } \\% = \\left(\\frac{\\text{Attended Classes}}{\\text{Total Classes}}\\right) \\times 100$$\n73: - **Safe Bunk Allowance** ($\\ge 75\\%$):\n74:   $$\\text{Safe Bunks} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{\\text{Attended} - 0.75 \\times \\text{Total}}{0.75} \\right\\rfloor$$\n75: - **Consecutive Attendance Needed to Escape Detention** ($< 75\\%$):\n76:   $$\\text{Classes Needed} = \\left\\lceil \\frac{0.75 \\times \\text{Total} - \\text{Attended}}{0.25} \\right\\rceil$$\n77: \n78: ### 2. 🔔 Real-Time Notification Bar & Time-to-Time Reminder Engine\n79: - **Sticky Top Notification Ticker**:\n80:   - Sits directly below the header with urgency color-coding (🔴 Critical Red, 🟡 Warning Amber, 🟣 Exam Purple).\n81:   - Automatically scans and surfaces upcoming deliverables (*“DBMS Normalization due in 2 days!”*), imminent exams (*“OOP / Java Exam in 12 days!”*), and attendance shortages (*“COA attendance is 60% — attend 21 classes!”*).\n82:   - Smooth auto-cycling progress line (cycles every 7 seconds) with manual previous `<` / next `>` arrows, pause/resume, and direct action jump buttons (*“Do It Now 🚀”*).\n83: - **Time-to-Time Periodic Reminders**:\n84:   - Configurable timer (1 min demo mode, 3 mins, 10 mins, 30 mins, 1 hour) that fires periodic check-in audio chimes and collegiate humor toasts.\n85:   - Native **Web Notification API** integration for desktop push notifications outside the browser tab.\n86: - **Notification Center Drawer**:\n87:   - Accessed via the 🔔 Bell icon in the top header with a live unread alert badge.\n88:   - Lists all pending tasks categorized by urgency with 1-click navigation.\n89: \n90: ### 3. 🎓 Academic Survival Score ($0 - 100$)\n91: - **Weighted Health Indicator**:\n92:   - Attendance Health ($45\\%$ weight)\n93:   - Assignment Backlog ($35\\%$ weight)\n94:   - Closest Exam Buffer ($20\\%$ weight)\n95: - Visualized with an animated SVG radial progress ring and collegiate ranking titles (*Academic Comeback King 🔥*, *Surviving on Caffeine ☕*, *God Help You 💀*).\n96: \n97: ---\n98: \n99: ## 📱 Mobile-First Features\n100: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
